/* The rates are shared constants: every function and method reads them and
   nothing can change them, so they live at the top level under permanently —
   the one kind of top-level data functions may see. A traveler's name is set
   at creation and never changes; crossings do. The mutable tally stays in
   play, because mutable top-level data is still invisible to functions —
   the example shows both halves of the rule. */

Define base-fare as 2 permanently.
Define per-weight as 1 permanently.
Define member-discount as 1 permanently.
Define storm-surge as 5 permanently.
Define storm-day as false permanently.

Define object traveler with (the text name permanently,
                             the number weight,
                             the fact member,
                             the number crossings):
    Bind number to fare:
        Define raw as base-fare + one's weight * per-weight.
        Define discounted as raw - member-discount when one's member, otherwise raw.
        Define surcharge as storm-surge when storm-day, otherwise 0.
        Return discounted + surcharge.
    Done.

    Bind number to cross:
        One's crossings becomes one's crossings + 1.
        Return cast one's fare.
    Done.
Done.

Bind text to rate-card:
    Define mood as "storm rates in effect" when storm-day, otherwise "calm rates".
    Return "base {base-fare}, per-weight {per-weight}, member discount {member-discount}, surge {storm-surge} — {mood}".
Done.

Bind void to play:
    State cast rate-card.
    State "".

    Define hopper as a new traveler { the name "Hopper", the weight 3, the member true, the crossings 0 }.
    Define wolf as a new traveler { the name "Wolf", the weight 9, the member false, the crossings 0 }.
    Define beaver as a new traveler { the name "Beaver", the weight 6, the member true, the crossings 0 }.

    Define collected as 0.
    Increment collected by cast hopper's cross.
    Increment collected by cast hopper's cross.
    Increment collected by cast wolf's cross.
    Increment collected by cast beaver's cross.

    For each who in a series of traveler with (hopper, wolf, beaver), repeat:
        Define crossing-word as "crossing" when who's crossings is 1, otherwise "crossings".
        State "{who's name}: {who's crossings} {crossing-word} at {cast who's fare} each".
    Done.
    State "".
    State "collected: {collected}".
Done.

Cast play.